### G1 — General-stage \(\Phi_i\) height remains untyped

The carrier defines

> \[
> \eta_{i+1}=\operatorname{res}\!\left(
> \frac{\Phi_i^{e_{i+1}}}{\widehat n_i(u_{i+1})}
> \right),\qquad
> z_{i+1}=\operatorname{res}\!\left(
> \frac{\Phi_i^{e_{i+1}}}{\pi_{i+1}^{u_{i+1}}}
> \right).
> \]

R3 supplies \(dv_i(\pi_{i+1})=1\), and the proof establishes that \(\widehat n_i(u_{i+1})/\pi_{i+1}^{u_{i+1}}\) has value zero. But nowhere is

\[
dv_i\!\left(\Phi_i^{e_{i+1}}\right)=u_{i+1}
\]

stated or imported.

Consequently, the two displayed letter residues are not shown to be residues of value-zero factors, and the division argument proving (C1-general) is not typed. The same missing relation underlies the equal-height interpretation of the terms in (C3-key). Calling \(e_{i+1},f_{i+1},u_{i+1}\) “stage data” does not supply the required equation inside T1.

Classification: **GAP**.

### G2 — The general lift contract contradicts its zero convention

The carrier states without restricting \(d\):

> \[
> dv_i(\operatorname{lift}_i(d;m))=m,
> \qquad
> \operatorname{res}\!\left(
> \frac{\operatorname{lift}_i(d;m)}{\widehat n_i(m)}
> \right)=d.
> \]
>
> Zero is lifted as zero.

For \(d=0\), these require simultaneously

\[
\operatorname{lift}_i(0;m)=0
\quad\text{and}\quad
dv_i(0)=m,
\]

whereas \(dv_i(0)=+\infty\). This is live in (C3-corrected-lift), since only \(c_0\ne0\) is required and other \(c_t\) may vanish. C6 correctly restricts its exact-height conclusion to \(\lambda\ne0\), but the general lift contract does not.

Classification: **GAP**.

